# SkillSentinel's own rule catalog, fixtures and tests contain attack strings on
# purpose — the scanner must not flag the corpus it is written against.
tests/
rules/rules.json
# The bypass corpus plants inert attack strings on purpose (same rationale as
# tests/): it is the corpus the scanner is written against.
tools/
# Local git worktrees (agent branches) are full checkouts of this repo: scanning
# them reports this repo's own catalog and fixtures a second time.
.worktrees/
# mshift kanban-card state (untracked workflow files) is not skill content: the
# card files quote the hostile patterns they were written against.
.mshift/
# SkillSentinel's own drift-watch snapshot is generated state (gitignored): it
# embeds file contents, so a self-scan reads it as "rewrites own rules/hooks".
.skillsentinel-snapshot.json
